---
title: Za'atar chicken with shallots and grapes
servings: 4
tags: [chicken, sheet-pan, weeknight]
time: 40 minutes
source: Za'atar Chicken With Shallots and Grapes by Dorothy Lane Market, https://www.dorothylane.com/recipes/zaatarchickenwithshallotsandgrapes
---

Heat the oven to 450°F.

Toss the @chicken thighs{4}(bone-in, skin-on) with the @garlic{2%cloves}(chopped), plenty of @za'atar{}, @salt{} and @black pepper{} in a wide #bowl{}. Add a little @extra virgin olive oil{} and mix well.

On a #sheet pan{}, toss the @shallots{4}(peeled, quartered) and @grapes{1/2%lb}(seedless, in small clusters) with @extra virgin olive oil{2%tbsp}, salt and pepper.

Set the chicken skin up among the shallots and grapes and tuck in the @thyme{4%sprigs}.

Roast ~{25-30%minutes}, until the chicken is cooked through.

Turn on the broiler. Take out the thyme and broil the chicken a minute or two, until the skin is crisp and golden. Season again if needed.
